If someone wants to be handheld every step of the way, there are plenty
of people in #nethack willing to do that.  I am not going to, and as
such I would prefer to keep my advice brief.  I believe people gain more
satisfaction from figuring things out themselves when possible.  I know
some don't, and are just completionists -- finish game, use walkthrough
when stuck, move on to next game.  But I'm not going to cater to those 
people; that can be someone else's job.

> And your advice was just plain bad -- there's no advantage to
