Until they fixate on #force, and never realize that a wand or spellbook in
hand right now is well worth the cost of an unknown potion.  There is no
shortage of daggers, but you must make sure to BUC-test anything you're
intending to wield; in the early game, getting an orcish dagger stuck to
your hand is highly inconvenient.  (While I doubt many people play
pettype:none, getting your pet killed by a falling rock trap early in
the game is certainly not uncommon; people should be able to play
without pets as well as with, even if they prefer having the pets.)

A few broken potions isn't _ever_ going to be what stops a less-skilled 
player from ascending.  This is part of the more sophisticated point I 
try to make.  And no, I do not like having to spell it out quite like this.

> In short, Janis is right; taking steps to ensure safety is a good
