My advice is designed to encourage people to attempt to reach that skill
level.  It's the "teach a man to fish" thing in a different form..., but 
it's a shame that people just can't get past the details to understand 
the principles I'm trying to convey.

Some of that, of course, is because I'm arguing against the "collective
wisdom" of players who learned to play without the advantages modern players 
have now -- and their gameplay suffered for it.  I see no reason new
players should have to suffer through that stage.  I think it is
perfectly possible to jump from "newbie" to "skilled" without wading
through the slog first.

